<title>MEXICO: Ahmsa says accused of dumping.</title>
<headline>Ahmsa says accused of dumping.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican steelmaker Altos Hornos de Mexico (AHMSA) said Tuesday it was the subject of a dumping investigation by Canadian authorities, following a formal complaint by Stelco Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;AHMSA is studying the dumping charge...involving Canadian imports of certain types of carbon steel plate from producers from Mexico, China, Poland, South Africa and Russia,&quot; the Mexican steel company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Stelco authorities said Monday the alleged dumping was harming Canadian producers by keeping prices low and hurting sales.</p>
<p>AHMSA said it will have a response to the charges by March 24.</p>
<p>((--Daniel Perez-Whitaker, Monterrey bureau +528 345-7617))</p>
